# Example settings for NovelAI. Copy to .env.novelai in the project root to use (this example file itself is not read).
# Keep API keys and URLs in the shared .env (or .secrets/novelai.env / environment variables); do not write them in this file.
# novelai_batch.py reads variables from environment variables and .env.novelai. Defining the same name in both raises an error.
# Variables and auxiliary settings placed in .env or .secrets in earlier versions can be migrated with `python -X utf8 scripts/novelai_batch.py env-migrate`.

# Character, style, and background prompt variables (used only when requested). Reference from request JSON as ${VARIABLE_NAME}.
# Editing and regeneration guide: docs/novelai-prompts/README.md
# NOVELAI_CHAR_MIO="1girl, light brown short bob hair, yellow hairclip, yellow hoodie over navy blazer"
# NOVELAI_STYLE_MAIN="clean lineart, soft colors, anime style"
# NOVELAI_BACKGROUND_CLASSROOM="classroom, desks, windows, daylight"

# Auxiliary settings read by novelai_compose.py (standard request JSON builder) and novelai_batch.py. Aside from the prompt variables above, only these four settings are read.
# Priority: CLI arguments > environment variables / .env.novelai > defaults.
# NOVELAI_QUALITY_TAGS="very aesthetic, masterpiece, no text"
# NOVELAI_UC_PRESET="heavy"
# NOVELAI_UC_PRESET_TEXT="lowres, bad anatomy"
# NOVELAI_CHECK_IDENTITY=1
